# Git Rules

## Objective

Commit, branch, and PR conventions for {{PROJECT_NAME}} ({{PROJECT_TYPE}}).

## Commits

Prefer Conventional Commits:

```
feat(scanner): detect pnpm lockfile as package manager evidence
fix(compiler): omit database section when none detected
```

### Examples (neutral)

```
feat(cli): add validate command for generated context
docs(context): clarify CI commented status
```

Do not use JWT/auth examples unless the project has an auth surface.

## Branches

- Prefer short-lived feature branches
- Protect the default branch according to team policy

## Pull requests

- Describe intent and test plan
- Do not claim CI is green if CI is absent or commented out (see deployment context)

